00:49:43.410 --> 00:49:45.660
- They can't prove anything? - No.

00:49:45.660 --> 00:49:48.610
Once they start asking questions, I...

00:49:48.610 --> 00:49:53.260
That's why I went to the city. I had to make sure that I hadn't overlooked anything in the apartment.

00:49:53.260 --> 00:49:55.650
Why didn't I report it in the first place?

00:49:55.650 --> 00:49:57.760
Why did I let you talk me into it?

00:49:57.760 --> 00:49:59.380
If it weren't for that Stewart girl...

00:50:00.060 --> 00:50:02.100
If they start asking questions and find her...

00:50:02.100 --> 00:50:03.180
Maybe they won't find it.

00:50:03.470 --> 00:50:05.470
We've taken care of everything else so far.

00:50:05.510 --> 00:50:07.010
If we have to, we'll take care of her too.

00:50:07.710 --> 00:50:09.310
And you're not helping matters acting this way.

00:50:33.520 --> 00:50:41.090
I could give her insulin shock treatments, shock treatments indicated in a case like hers.

00:50:41.090 --> 00:50:48.500
I could give her four injections, then with the last one, an overdose, no one would ever know the difference.

00:50:48.500 --> 00:50:52.970
Then we'd be safe. No matter what the district attorney's office found, we'd be safe.

00:50:52.970 --> 00:51:00.000
They'd have nothing on us, Richard. We could get married then. You'd be yourself again, Richard. We'd find...

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:07.160
peace and quiet here just the two you don't think I do it do you why not is her life more important

00:51:07.160 --> 00:51:13.420
than ours I've had enough look Elaine I can't go on like this things keep piling up first it was

00:51:13.420 --> 00:51:18.610
Margaret then tricking that child so that she'd forget then convincing her that she was insane

00:51:18.610 --> 00:51:30.000
there's a limit beyond which even I can't go Richard

00:51:31.310 --> 00:51:35.990
Remember the first night I came here, remember?

00:51:35.990 --> 00:51:54.580
We were in front of the fireplace with a sick headache.

00:51:54.580 --> 00:51:56.380
The lights were out.

00:51:56.910 --> 00:52:00.000
You didn't hear me when I knocked and I opened the door...

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:05.980
I said, "Oh, it's you, Miss Jordan."

00:52:05.980 --> 00:52:10.200
You called me Miss Jordan then, remember?

00:52:10.200 --> 00:52:14.320
I told you I had to see you about Mrs. Penny's prescription.

00:52:14.320 --> 00:52:16.320
You talked to me and you saw that I was tired

00:52:16.320 --> 00:52:19.440
and you asked me if I wouldn't have a drink.

00:52:19.440 --> 00:52:22.500
I hesitated and you said,

00:52:22.500 --> 00:52:25.920
"I won't bite your head off, Miss Jordan."

00:52:25.920 --> 00:52:29.250
We had a drink, remember?

00:52:31.630 --> 00:52:36.740
sat here for a long time and then suddenly you left and you said your headache was gone

00:52:36.740 --> 00:52:54.620
and you asked me about my family and I told you and we both laughed. Remember? You took

00:52:54.620 --> 00:52:59.120
me in your arms. I know you remember that.

00:53:01.820 --> 00:53:25.930
I won't do it. I won't do it a minute. I'm coming on the bed. No told me at the

00:53:25.930 --> 00:53:30.000
hospital. I'd find you here. I didn't expect to see you so soon. Mr.

00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:33.440
Sir O'Neil, I thought you'd phone me if there were any developments.

00:53:33.680 --> 00:53:34.680
I had to serve the papers.

00:53:35.500 --> 00:53:36.020
Oh, yes?

00:53:36.420 --> 00:53:37.640
Coroner's inquest subpoena.

00:53:38.030 --> 00:53:38.670
Now it's legal.

00:53:39.280 --> 00:53:42.380
What did the coroner find?

00:53:44.240 --> 00:53:45.580
Your wife was murdered, doctor.

00:53:48.260 --> 00:53:57.460
Oh, sure.

00:53:58.230 --> 00:53:58.630
Yes, sir.

00:54:06.270 --> 00:54:08.570
He was beaten over the head, suffered an explosive fracture.

00:54:08.870 --> 00:54:10.470
Death was practically instantaneous.

00:54:12.350 --> 00:54:15.540
This prowler you told me about, you think he did it?

00:54:16.190 --> 00:54:16.890
Seems so.

00:54:17.680 --> 00:54:18.760
He clubbed Mrs. Harwood.

00:54:19.340 --> 00:54:20.680
Your wife went out the same way.

00:54:21.430 --> 00:54:21.790
Pattern.

00:54:22.300 --> 00:54:23.720
Killers usually follow a pattern.

00:54:24.910 --> 00:54:27.170
You don't know how she was killed.

00:54:27.760 --> 00:54:28.520
I mean, the weapon.

00:54:28.930 --> 00:54:30.000
She was struck with a candlestick.

00:54:31.370 --> 00:54:33.460
A candlestick? Are you sure?

00:54:33.460 --> 00:54:34.920
A heavy silver one.

00:54:34.920 --> 00:54:36.510
How can you know?

00:54:36.510 --> 00:54:37.510
Microscope.

00:54:37.510 --> 00:54:39.780
There were particles of silver in the wound.

00:54:39.780 --> 00:54:41.830
They told us it was a silver object.

00:54:41.830 --> 00:54:43.910
There were bits of wax mixed in with the silver.

00:54:43.910 --> 00:54:46.340
They told us it was a candlestick.

00:54:46.340 --> 00:54:48.340
Must have been a heavy candlestick to have done the damage.

00:54:48.340 --> 00:54:55.820
Just routine, Doctor.

00:54:55.820 --> 00:54:59.280
A criminal doesn't have much of a chance these days, does he?

00:54:59.280 --> 00:54:59.800
No, sir.

00:55:03.290 --> 00:55:06.800
By the way, do you have any silver candlesticks at the lodge?

00:55:06.800 --> 00:55:08.130
We might have.

00:55:08.130 --> 00:55:10.260
I'd like your permission to go through the house.

00:55:10.260 --> 00:55:14.280
The murderer may have left the candlestick behind, in which case we'll get fingerprints.

00:55:14.280 --> 00:55:17.840
If he got rid of the weapon, we may be able to find the mate.

00:55:17.840 --> 00:55:19.180
Then we'll know what to look for.

00:55:19.180 --> 00:55:20.560
Of course, go right ahead.

00:55:20.560 --> 00:55:23.380
Thanks.

00:55:23.380 --> 00:55:26.020
Now, if we can find the candlestick, our troubles are over.

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:36.690
the way when did you see mrs cross last alive i mean oh a couple of weeks before she was killed

00:55:37.240 --> 00:55:45.610
why can you place a little more definitely i think so things have been piling up around here

00:55:45.610 --> 00:55:53.080
and i needed a change so i drove down to point lobus on a friday night anyone see you i don't

00:55:53.080 --> 00:56:00.000
think so why we're trying to fix the exact time of her death well i'm not sure anyone saw me

00:56:00.570 --> 00:56:05.590
I drove down there on Friday night, left there around 9.30 Saturday night.

00:56:06.630 --> 00:56:08.330
Well, it's not too important.

00:56:11.660 --> 00:56:14.480
Naturally, I want to do everything I can to help you, Mr. O'Neill.

00:56:14.850 --> 00:56:16.970
